INT. WILLOWBROOK CRICKET PAVILION - RAIN DELAY - DAY

Dark wood. A bar with brass taps. Team photographs from a century of afternoons. Rain hammers the tin roof so hard the room rings. Through the long window, the pitch is a lake.

BHASKAR VENKATARAMAN, 40s, the home captain, in whites stained green at the knee, stands at the window, arms crossed. He is silent. He has been silent for forty minutes.

LORD WILLOUGHBY "BILLY" FANSHAWE, 60s, the visiting captain, a blazer and a cravat, sits in a leather armchair with a tumbler of whisky and a newspaper. He turns a page. He sips.

WILLOUGHBY
Awful weather.

BHASKAR
Mm.

WILLOUGHBY
Might be a draw.

BHASKAR
Mm.

WILLOUGHBY
I say, are you going to say anything other than "Mm"?

BHASKAR
I am conserving words.

WILLOUGHBY
For what?

BHASKAR
For when you apologize.

Willoughby lowers the paper. Studies him over his glasses.

WILLOUGHBY
Apologize? For what, pray?

BHASKAR
For the run-out.

WILLOUGHBY
Ah. That.

BHASKAR
Yes. That.

WILLOUGHBY
It was a perfectly legal run-out.

BHASKAR
It was a gentleman's agreement. We had it. You broke it.

WILLOUGHBY
Gentlemen's agreements are a bit rich, aren't they? Between you and me?

Rain thunders. Somewhere a gutter overflows.

FLORENCE OKONKWO-BEAUFORT, 70s, the club umpire, in a white coat and a flat cap, pushes in through the side door with a golf umbrella that is not helping. She stamps her boots.

FLORENCE
Gentlemen! Ground's unplayable. I've called it.

BHASKAR
Thank you, Florence.

WILLOUGHBY
Dreadful, Florence. Utterly dreadful.

FLORENCE
Don't you "dreadful" me, Billy Fanshawe. I saw that run-out.

WILLOUGHBY
Madam --

BHASKAR
She saw it.

WILLOUGHBY
Thank you, Bhaskar, I can speak for myself --

FLORENCE
I've umpired for thirty-one years. I've seen every kind of foul play. But I've never seen a man do it with such a smile.

WILLOUGHBY
(stiffly)
It was an honest mistake.

BHASKAR
(to Florence)
It wasn't.

FLORENCE
(to Bhaskar)
It wasn't.

Willoughby sets down his glass. The ice clinks. He stands, too fast, and knocks his knee against the table.

WILLOUGHBY
Very well! I concede! It was a bad piece of sportsmanship!

Silence. Rain. The old photographs watch from the walls.

BHASKAR
And?

WILLOUGHBY
And... I apologize.

BHASKAR
To whom?

WILLOUGHBY
(through his teeth)
To you, Captain Venkataraman.

BHASKAR
And?

WILLOUGHBY
And to Florence.

FLORENCE
And?

WILLOUGHBY
And... to the game.

The tin roof crackles. Bhaskar's mouth twitches. Florence shakes her umbrella, spraying them both.

BHASKAR
Thank you.

FLORENCE
Tea?

WILLOUGHBY
Whisky.

FLORENCE
Tea.

She pours three cups from a brown pot. They sit around the table, three old foes in damp white, listening to the water drown the pitch.
